        <p>This REFINED COSTUME</p>
        <p>can be had in thret qualities at 8/11.10/6. and 12/11 There's no difference in all the making, only in the quality of the cloth. Albeit. the 8/1 1 quality can he thoroughly recommended. Only a limited number left. Made in Black or R Navy V.C.C. Cheviot 40/ Serge. COAT : 32 in. long—sac back --Chesterfield front—bell sleeves —well-bound seams. SKIRT: Plain back- side fastenir*--fiinish, lovely. Carriage 6d. extra.</p>
        <p>ALAN St AUBYN • (Author of" A Fellow of Trinity,"</p>
        <p>Princess Louise Augusta of Schleswig-Hol.steine the youngest datighter',. of Princess Christian, closely resembles her mother in the active inte- rest she takes in everything that has charity as its object. The Princess, who lives a good deal in London, has na infrequently been a substi- tute, for Princess' Christian When the latter's numerous engagements have been more than she could personally fulfil. She is considered by many to be one of the handsomest of the King's elder nieces, and was much admired when some few years ago she often appeared at the Court of Berlin.</p>
