      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-06_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>AFTEnNooN Cows.</head>
        <p>AFTEnNooN Cows.</p>
        <p>Our sketch shews an afternoon gown of grey taffetas. The bodice has an oblong opening in front, edged with little knife-pleated frills, and discloses an ivory vest, crossed by straps of pale- blue velvet, terminating in tiny crystal buttons. A small round yoke appears above the bodice, embroidered in pale bltio faded mauve, and</p>
        <p>silver. Leg-of-mutton sleeves end in close- fitting cuffs, on which the straps of velvet again appear. The skirt is very full, being gathered at the waist, and is ornamented by three rows of the knife-pleated frills. The belt is of blue velvet to match the straps.</p>
        <p>GROWING OLD BEAIITIFTTLLY. 'The woman who grows old beautifully—whose , face is as pleasant in old age as youth—has had certain receipts. Hero are some of them: She learns how to forget disagreeable thin. She did not give way to her nerves, and inflict them on her friends. She mastered the art of sayipg pleasant things. , She did not expect too much from her friends. She made whatever work she had to do con- genial. She did not lose sight of her illusions, and would not think all the world wicked and un- kind. She helped the miserable, and sympathised with the sorrowful. To-DAY'S RECIPE. •</p>
        <p>_ JERIJSALM AUTICUOKES A L'ITALIENNE. —Wash and peel the artichokes, shaping them like pears of uniform size. Butter a stewpan with 20z. of butter, :nd arrange the artichokes in circles. Strew over some pepper, salt, and lemon juice; pour a quarter of a Dint of good gravy over them. out the lid on. and simmer tor imit-an-nour, uastiug them occa- sionally. They should colour a deep yellow. Serve with a rich white sauce round them.</p>
