        <p>the following offer was made by the Helsby Cables Limited: Provided the Council would for a period of five years give them the natural overflow fAorn the Council's well, they would (1) lay a four inch main from the 'pumping station to the site of the cable works : (2) pay an annual acknowledgement of £1 ; (3) pump from the cable works to the Council's reservoir for five years at the rate of 240 hours a year, at such times as the Coun- cil may from time to time require ; the committee con- sidered these proposals together with alternative methods for meeting the shortage? and it was resolved to accept the Helsby Cable Company's offer with the promise that the cable should pump at the rate of 6,000 gallows per hour. The decision of the committee was communicated to the Helsby Cables Limited, who had written signifying their acceptance of the terms. Mr. Linaker moved the adoption of the report. The decision which had been arrived at was one which would be of great advantage to the Helsby- people and would relieve the Council for five years, from having to provide duplicate engines. Mr. Pilling seconded. There was no doubt the Council would benefit by the arrangements. The proposition was carried.</p>
