        <head>THERAPION.</head>
        <p>THERAPION.</p>
        <p>This preparation is unquestionably one of the most gen- uine and rellakie Patent Medicines ever introduced, and has we understand, been used in the Continental Hospitals by Ricord, Rostan, Jobert. Veipeau, Maisonneuve. the well- known Chassaignac, and indeed by all who arc regarded as authorities in such matters, betiding the celebrated Lane- mend, and Roux. by whom it was some time since uniformly adopted, and that it is worthy the attention of those who require such a remedy we think there is no doubt. From the time of Aristotle downwards a potent agent in the removal of these diseases has, like the fame! philosopher's stone been the object of search of some hopeful generous minds ; and far beyond the mere power—if such could ever have been discovered—of transmuting the baser metal Imo gold is surely the discovery of a remedy so potent as to replenish the falling energies in the one case, and In the other so effectually, speedily and safely to expel from the system the poisons of acquired or inherited disease in all their proteau forms as to leave no taint or trace behind, Such is the new French Remedy THIERAPION, which may certainly rank with. if not take precedence of. many of the discoveries of our day, about which no little Batentation and noise have been amide, and the extensive and ever-Increas- ing demand that has been created for this medicine wherever introduced appears to prove that It is destined to cast int r oblivion all those questionable remedies that were formerly the sole reliance of medical men. Therapion may be obtained of the principal chemists and merchants throughout the world —" Diamond fields Advertiser -Kimberley —For par- ticulars of Thersploll, send stamped, addressed envelope to 'MR. If. JOHNSON, 43. HOLFORD 5,2., LONDON, W.O.</p>
