        <p>ZAM-BUK CUBES A BOY'S SORE HEAD.</p>
        <p>Warrington mothers who will all be interested in an affair reported by the "Wigan Examiner." It concerns the remarkable cure by Zam-Buk of the three- year-old son of Mr. John Mawdsley, of 451, Bickershaw Lane, Abram, near Wigan. For twelve months the poor child suffered with irritating scalp sores, a complaint which"often attacks adults as well as young children. Only Zam-Buk was able to grow new, healthy skin in place of the mass of itching sores, and make the scalp clearr and sweet.</p>
        <p>lowit</p>
        <p>"For the first eighteen months of his life," said Mr. Mawdsley to the reporter, "my baby was as healthy as could be desired. Then a rash broke out on his head, and soon small pimples formed. These seemed to fill up with water, and they became so irritable that we couldn't keep his fingers away from Master Mandsley, Wigan. (Photo). them. Consequently, his head became one mass of sores. He was in perfect misery, and his mother and myself were at our wits' end to know what we could get to relieve his sufferings. We tried four different doctors, but to no avail. Neither salve nor medicine did him any good, and his life continued to be a perfect misery until he was nearly three years old. Then we saw Zam-Buk advertised, and got a free sample. Such an improvemcnt was seen after the application of even so small a quantity, that we got a is. id. box and persevered with the applications. As we rubbed it in the irritation was allayed, and the scalp by degrees assumed a healthier tone. The child was soon able to rest better, and now, thanks to Zam-Buk, he has been completely cured. He is now as healthy-looking a boy as can be found in the country. Both my wife and I seize every opportunity to tell of Zam-Buk's wonderful healing power, and we hope other parents will be guided by our experience."</p>
        <p>Zam-Buk makes the skin healthy and soft. It is unequalled for running sores, sore heads, inflamed or irritating patches, chafing, eczema, boils, ulcers, bad legs, piles, diseased ankles, sore backs, fester- ing sores, poisoned wounds, cuts, bruises, burns, .scalds, sprains, stiffness, pimples, sore throat and chest, and nerve pains. Of all chemists, or direct from the Zam- Buk Co. 4, Red Cross-street, London, E.G. for Is. Co., or 2s. 9d. per box (2s. 9r19 . box contains nearly four times the Is. lid).</p>
