      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-06_WidnesExaminer_art0089" n="art0089">
        <head>Daring Sex.</head>
        <p>The Daring Sex.</p>
        <p>Never was a saying more truly applied in VA ease of riders of the fair sex than that of mortals rushing in where angels fear to tread! In any of the towns, now that the season is under way, the startlinv acts of female cyclists are almost enough to make one's hair stand on end. You will see them turn corners like an express on a curve, dash into main thoroughfares congested with traffic of all kinds, worm in between omnibuses and electric tramcars or heavy drays, the meanwhile showing a most complacent disregard for the rule of the road. Is it not a little remarkable Why the weaker sex (?) should possess such a spirit of daring, when the male cyclist as a rule is careful to keep the 'Pace down and wait his opportunities without taking any risks when wheeling through the traffic? Probably if a census were taken of the fatal and Other accidents that had happened since the ladies took to cycling, it would be found that the figures Were overwhelmingly on the side of the fair ones. Side-slip appears to be an unknown quantity, yet lu the majority of cases where a spill has proved fatal, the roads have invariably been in a greasy condition. Such terrible accidents, however, make little or no impression upon these "angels on 'wheels."</p>
        <p>These characteristics, however, are more to be Observed among lady cyclists who restrict their Cycling to our parks and the suburban roads of our big towns. The wheelwoman who travels further afield is quite a different person, especially if she rides with an escort. The longer the journey the znore serious the work, and though the pleasure is taorc yet it has a steadying effect upon cyclists of both sexes. Get out into the country is always the advice of the seasoned cyclist to the young rider, and it applies to the lady cyclist just the same as to her brothers, only we may add a further injunc- tion in her case, which is "and take an escort."</p>
        <p>... ' , ice• _____,• i...-. ...• coo ~ ...- .. . ..-1 `\.. - 1 ) A , - Air , ~, %,.....:‘;‘, _ 71:2----, ~.....</p>
