        <p>MUNICIPAL BYE-ELEC HON, 1901 TO THE ELECTORS OF b'V. AUSTIN'S WARD, FELLOW (Jun axe,— In view of the great netd for Direct and Independent Labour Representation on all governing bodies, I have been invited to contest St. Austin's Ward at this bye. election. The invitation has been extended to me by a large number of Residents in the Ward,also by the Warrington Branch of the Gas Workers and i,eneral Labourer's Union,and endorsed by the local Labour Representation Committee. I therefore take this opportunity of stating my views. I believe in absointe Pnrity of Munleipil Government. I strongly favour a futther extension of kfunlalp‘l Enter- prise. Trades Union Rate of Wages and an Right-hour Day tonal' Corporation Workmen.directiemployment of Labour by the Corporation, the feeding of under-fed School Children, Abolition of all Insanitary Property under the Working Classes' Dwellings Acts Free Education, Immediate construction of a healthy and commodious Lodging House on modern principle., Free Baths, Cheaper Gas, Branch Libraries, Useful work for the Unemployed, Taxing of Land Values, a Stringent Fair Wage Clause in all Corporation Contracts, Reduction of Train Fares. is a Labour man, I shall work for any scheme which has for its object the Improvement of the conditions of the Working Classes, and to this end my policy wilt always be directed. Yours sincerely. EDWARD HORROMES, 3. Elaine street. Warrington.</p>
        <p>yE:I, I KNOW I have only got a Small Shop, but a Small Shop means a small rent and I GIVII CUSTOISIBIIS the BICYBPIT of it. Just try me once, you are sure to be satisfied and will become a regular customer. Anything whatever in the Cycle Line. , What about RNAMILLIING and PLATING your CYCLB, I can make it look like new, or do you want some small repair executing. no job too small, or are you thinking of baying a new Cycle built to your own order. You cannot do better than get my price. I will deal with you reasonably. Jost try me.— CANNIILL. HESKETH at., off Liverpool rd., Sankey Bridges Warrington. Cars stop opposite the street.</p>
