        <p>• COMMERCIAL. FAILURES.—According to " Kemp's., Mercantile Gazette," the to number of Commercial vailnres recorded in England and Wales during the week ending Friday, April 2Sth, was 76, viz. :—New bankruptcy proceedings published in the London. Gazette, 41; deeds of arrangement registered, 35. The respective numbers in the corresponding week of last year were: Bankruptcies, 115; deeds of arrangement 130—total 245; being a decrease of 169. The total number of commercial failures recorded during the 17 weeks of the present year is 3,108; the total number recorded in the corresponding 17 weeks of last year was 3,003, showing an increase of 103. WHAT LAW OFFICERS DRAW. The Secretary of the Treasury has informed Mr. J. 'H. Whitley, M.P., that the fees (including clerks' fees) paidtto the English law officers of the Crown last year were as follows :—Attorney-General—Salary, £7,000 ; fees, £5,993 14s. 43.; total, £12,993 14s. 43. Solicitor- General—Salary, £6,000; fees, £3,748 17s. 3d..; total, £9,748 17s. 3d.</p>
