        <p>PIRIKETH V. MOORE.—Played at Moore on Saturday. Score : MOORE. PENKETII. Rev. T. T. Lee-Jones b J. E. Shoobridge b S. Williams 0 Taylor S. Taylor c Davies b A. Cmgg b S. Taylor 0 Shoobridge C. B. Allan c Dumbill b H. Davies c H. Taylor Williams J. Forster c Warburton b T. Ray b Forster Shoo bridge H. Taylor b Shoobridge 3 A. J. Williams b S. W.Antrobus b Shoobridge 0 Taylor J. Smith b Shoobridge... 0 R.E.Warburton run out 7 J. Millington c Dumbill A. Hodgkinson c Lee- b Shoobridge C. Kile•aw not out 4 3. Kirkham run out ... 0 G.Gandy b Shoobridge 0 J. Jones not out Extras Total Secular Meeting at Warrington. A meeting was held in the Druids Hall, Sankey- street on Tuesday night, at which a lecture was de- livered by Mr. Ward, Liverpool, on " From Wesleyan ' ' pulpit to secular platform." Mr, A. Grimshaw pre- sided over a fair attendance. Mr. Ward in his address explained his reasons for leaving the Wesleyan pulpit and becoming a lecturer on behalf of secularism. One of the chief reasons, he said, why pe gave up Chris- tianity was not because he read books against Chris- tianity but because the last books he could read in support of that belief in themselves disproved the belief. The Bible is full of contradictions, atrocities absurdities, inpurities and indecencies. He did not believe in a future and preached that it was better to try and make this earth a paradise than to shrive after a paradise after death. At the conclusion of the address questions were invited, and in answer to Mr. Elwell, the Lecturer said he did not attribute the existence of the universe to blind chance. The universe was composed of matter and force which had always existed. Matter and force could not be destroyed, and were therefore eternal.— A vote of thanks to the lecturer concluded the Meeting</p>
